==Latin==

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*preyH-}}
From {{prefix|la|prō-}} {{der|la|itc-pro|*prijos}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*priHós}}, akin to {{cog|en|free}}.

Other suggestions are:
* for {{m|la||*prōprīvus}}, from {{m|la|prīvus}} or ultimately from this root.
* for {{m|la||*prōpatrius}}, from {{pre|la|prō|pater|nocat=1}}, meaning “from one's forefathers”, taking {{cog|grc|προπάτωρ|t=forefather}} as comparison.

